<BaseLayout title="Theory Overview" description="A 5-minute introduction to Spatial Displacement Theory - the core concepts, key equations, and revolutionary insights.">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-500 mb-4">
        <a href="/theory" class="hover:text-sdt-primary-600">Theory</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span>Overview</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-display font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">
        What is Spatial Displacement Theory?
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-slate-600">
        A 5-minute introduction to the core concepts
      </p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">
        <span>Reading time: ~5 min</span>
        <span>&bull;</span>
        <span>Last updated: December 2025</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-slate prose-lg max-w-none">
      <h2>The Central Question</h2>
      <p>
        For a century, we've described atoms with probability waves, particles with intrinsic "spin,"
        and gravity as curved spacetime. These frameworks work spectacularly well&mdash;but they don't connect.
        Quantum mechanics and general relativity remain fundamentally incompatible.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Spatial Displacement Theory asks a different question:</strong>
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        What if space isn't empty, and particles aren't points?
      </blockquote>

      <h2>The Core Insight</h2>
      <p>
        Instead of starting with quantum postulates or curved spacetime, SDT begins with three simple axioms:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Space is filled</strong> with an incompressible medium called "spation"&mdash;Planck-scale
          particles that transmit pressure instantaneously.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Matter is shape</strong>&mdash;particles are stable toroidal vortices that displace
          spation from their volume.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Forces are shadows</strong>&mdash;when two bodies partially block each other from the
          ambient CMB pressure, the resulting pressure imbalance pushes them together.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p>
        From these axioms, everything follows. Gravity, electromagnetism, atomic spectra, nuclear
        binding&mdash;all emerge from geometry and pressure gradients.
      </p>

      <h2>The Master Equation</h2>
      <p>
        All of SDT is captured in one equation:
      </p>

      <div class="equation">
        <p class="text-center font-mono text-lg">
          &nabla; &middot; [K<sub>bulk</sub> &nabla;&Delta;(x)] = -&kappa; &rho;<sub>disp</sub>(x) (1 - E(x,n&#770;))
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>Where:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>K<sub>bulk</sub></strong> = 4.6&times;10<sup>113</sup> Pa (spation bulk modulus)</li>
        <li><strong>&rho;<sub>disp</sub></strong> = displacement density (matter excludes spation)</li>
        <li><strong>E(x,n&#770;)</strong> = directional occlusion function (mutual shadowing)</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        This single equation replaces:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Newton's law of gravitation</li>
        <li>Coulomb's law</li>
        <li>Schr&ouml;dinger equation</li>
        <li>Einstein field equations</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The Universal k-Law</h2>
      <p>
        One of SDT's most striking results is that orbital velocities follow a universal formula
        across <strong>53 orders of magnitude</strong> in scale:
      </p>

      <div class="equation">
        <p class="text-center font-mono text-xl">
          v(r) = (c/k) &times; &radic;(R/r)
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>
        Where k is a scale factor that ranges from 137 (hydrogen atom) to 10<sup>5</sup> (planetary systems).
        The same formula describes:
      </p>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>System</th>
            <th>k value</th>
            <th>Scale</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Hydrogen electron</td>
            <td>137.036</td>
            <td>10<sup>-11</sup> m</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Planetary orbits</td>
            <td>~59,000</td>
            <td>10<sup>11</sup> m</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Stellar systems</td>
            <td>~10<sup>4</sup></td>
            <td>10<sup>13</sup> m</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Galactic orbits</td>
            <td>~10<sup>5</sup></td>
            <td>10<sup>21</sup> m</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>What Makes SDT Different?</h2>

      <h3>Not an interpretation</h3>
      <p>
        SDT isn't an interpretation of quantum mechanics (like Copenhagen or Many-Worlds).
        It's a <strong>replacement</strong>. There are no wavefunctions in SDT&mdash;electrons
        are extended toroidal structures with measurable size (~10<sup>-21</sup> m).
      </p>

      <h3>Not a modification</h3>
      <p>
        SDT isn't Modified Newtonian Dynamics (MOND) or modified gravity. It's a fundamentally
        different mechanism: gravity arises from <strong>pressure screening</strong>, not curved
        spacetime or modified force laws.
      </p>

      <h3>Deterministic, not probabilistic</h3>
      <p>
        All "quantum randomness" in SDT is measurement limitation from vortex size, not
        fundamental indeterminacy. In principle, all particle positions and velocities
        are well-defined.
      </p>

      <h2>Validated Results</h2>
      <p>
        SDT has been rigorously tested against experimental data:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Atomic fine structure:</strong> Matches QED predictions to &lt;0.1%</li>
        <li><strong>Planetary accelerations:</strong> All 8 planets derived to &lt;0.5% without G or M</li>
        <li><strong>Stellar parameters:</strong> 50+ main sequence stars validated</li>
        <li><strong>CMB redshift:</strong> z = 1089 derived exactly from pressure horizon</li>
        <li><strong>BAO scale:</strong> 147 Mpc acoustic oscillation from geometric structure</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        <a href="/papers/benchmarks">See all 24 benchmarks &rarr;</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Revolutionary Claims</h2>

      <h3>No dark matter needed</h3>
      <p>
        Flat galactic rotation curves emerge from "disk eclipse saturation"&mdash;the occlusion
        function E(r) becomes radius-invariant for disk geometry, naturally producing the
        observed flat rotation curves without invisible matter.
      </p>

      <h3>G and M are derived quantities</h3>
      <p>
        The gravitational parameter &beta; = GM is not fundamental. It equals c&sup2;R/k&sup2;,
        where R is the body's radius and k is its scale factor. "Mass" is just geometry.
      </p>

      <h3>c is not the ultimate speed limit</h3>
      <p>
        The speed of light is the electromagnetic propagation limit in spation, not a mechanical
        speed limit. Bound protons in nuclei may orbit at 10-100&times; the speed of light,
        which is required for strong binding.
      </p>

      <h2>Where to Go Next</h2>

